Then:
```
def milnorLeviCivitaData (m) (b) : LeviCivitaData m b := { nabla := milnorConnection m b, torsion_free := milnorConnection_torsionFree m b, metric_compatible := milnorConnection_metricCompatible m b }

theorem leviCivitaExists (m) (b) : LeviCivitaExistenceStatement m b := ⟨milnorConnection m b, ⟨milnorConnection_torsionFree m b, milnorConnection_metricCompatible m b⟩⟩
```

bracketInvariant + equivalence with mean:
```
def bracketInvariant (m) (b) : Prop := ∀ X Y Z, m.form (b.bracket X Y) Z + m.form Y (b.bracket X Z) = 0

theorem milnorConnection_eq_mean_iff (m) (b) :
    milnorConnection m b = (meanConnection b).nabla ↔ bracketInvariant m b := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    have hlc : IsLeviCivita m b (meanConnection b).nabla := by
      rw [← h]
      exact ⟨milnorConnection_torsionFree m b, milnorConnection_metricCompatible m b⟩
    exact (meanConnection_isMetricCompatible_iff m b).mp hlc.2
  · intro h
    have hlcMean : IsLeviCivita m b (meanConnection b).nabla := by
      exact ⟨(meanConnection b).torsion_free, (meanConnection_isMetricCompatible_iff m b).mpr h⟩
    exact (leviCivita_nabla_unique m b ⟨milnorConnection_torsionFree m b, milnorConnection_metricCompatible m b⟩ hlcMean).symm
```
meanConnection b : AbstractConnection ℝ V — has .torsion_free field ✓.

Also the curvature connection: 
```
noncomputable def milnorAbstractConnection (m) (b) : AbstractConnection ℝ V := { nabla := milnorConnection m b, lie := b, torsion_free := milnorConnection_torsionFree m b }
```
and then `milnorCurvatureOperator := (milnorAbstractConnection m b).toCurvatureOperator` — with the skew/Bianchi inherited ✓. And downstream: ricci_symm will use milnorLeviCivitaData.

