```lean
/-- **Scalar curvature in any orthonormal frame**: `scalarCurvature K m.toScalarContractionData
= ∑ i, ricci K (f i) (f i)` for every orthonormal basis `f`. This is the naturality /
coordinate statement: the D7/Stage1 scalar contraction, computed through the metric's
raising map, agrees with the frame sum of the Ricci diagonal for *any* orthonormal frame. -/
theorem scalarCurvature_eq_sum_ricci_basis (m : MetricData V ι) (K : CurvatureOperator ℝ V)
    (f : Module.Basis ι ℝ V) (hf : ∀ i j, m.form (f i) (f j) = if i = j then 1 else 0) :
    scalarCurvature K m.toScalarContractionData = ∑ i : ι, ricci K (f i) (f i) := by
