```
/-- The chart connection packaged as an `AbstractConnection` with the zero coordinate
bracket; `toCurvatureOperator` yields the D7/Stage1 curvature operator with the checked
first-pair skew-symmetry and first Bianchi identities. -/
noncomputable def chartAbstractConnection (c : ChartMetricCoefficients ι) :
    AbstractConnection ℝ (ι → ℝ) where
  nabla := nablaOf c
  lie := LieBracketData.zero
  torsion_free := by
    intro X Y
    simpa [LieBracketData.zero] using chartTorsionFree_form c X Y

/-- The D7/Stage1 curvature operator of the chart Christoffel connection. -/
noncomputable def chartCurvatureOperator (c : ChartMetricCoefficients ι) :
    CurvatureOperator ℝ (ι → ℝ) :=
  (chartAbstractConnection c).toCurvatureOperator
```
And a theorem: the chart curvature evaluates: R(X,Y)Z = ∇_X∇_YZ − ∇_Y∇_XZ (bracket zero):
```
theorem chartCurvatureOperator_apply (c) (X Y Z : ι → ℝ) :
    chartCurvatureOperator c X Y Z =
      nablaOf c X (nablaOf c Y Z) - nablaOf c Y (nablaOf c X Z) := by
  rw [chartCurvatureOperator, AbstractConnection.toCurvatureOperator_apply,
    AbstractConnection.curvature_apply]
  simp [chartAbstractConnection, LieBracketData.zero]
```
